{"name":"Semolina Pudding","hex":"#ffe8c7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"semolina pudding","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft dessert made by boiling a mixture of semolina, sugar and flavourings in milk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/semolina_pudding"}],"entries":[{"title":"Semolina pudding","blocks":[{"text":"Semolina pudding or semolina porridge is a porridge-type pudding made from semolina, which is cooked with milk, or a mixture of milk and water, or just water. It is often served with sugar, cocoa powder, cinnamon, raisins, fruit, or syrup. It is similar to grain based halva or halawa. A similar consistency to rice pudding can also be made by using more semolina and by baking, rather than boiling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Griessbrei.jpg/330px-Griessbrei.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semolina_pudding"},{"title":"Semolina","blocks":[{"text":"Semolina is a coarse flour traditionally made from durum wheat. Its high protein and gluten content make it especially suitable for pasta."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Sa_semolina_far.jpg/330px-Sa_semolina_far.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semolina"},{"title":"Pudding","blocks":[{"text":"Pudding is a food which can either be a dessert or a savoury dish. In the United States, pudding means a sweet, milk-based dessert similar in consistency to egg-based custards, instant custards or a mousse, often commercially set using cornstarch, gelatin or similar coagulating agent. These puddings are known in some Commonwealth countries as custards if they are egg-thickened, as blancmange if starch-thickened, and as jelly if gelatin-based. Pudding in America may also refer to other dishes such as bread pudding and rice pudding, although typically these names derive from their origin as British dishes. The modern American meaning of pudding as dessert has evolved from the original almost exclusive use of the term to describe savoury dishes, specifically those created using a process similar to that used for sausages, in which meat and other ingredients in mostly liquid form are encased and then steamed or boiled to set the contents."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Blanc-manger_on_glass_platter%2C_full_view.jpg/330px-Blanc-manger_on_glass_platter%2C_full_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pudding"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/N%C3%ADzk%C3%A9_Tatry%2C_chata_gener%C3%A1la_Milana_Rastislava_%C5%A0tef%C3%A1nika_-_krupicov%C3%A1_ka%C5%A1e.JPG/500px-N%C3%ADzk%C3%A9_Tatry%2C_chata_gener%C3%A1la_Milana_Rastislava_%C5%A0tef%C3%A1nika_-_krupicov%C3%A1_ka%C5%A1e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/N%C3%ADzk%C3%A9_Tatry%2C_chata_gener%C3%A1la_Milana_Rastislava_%C5%A0tef%C3%A1nika_-_krupicov%C3%A1_ka%C5%A1e.JPG/1280px-N%C3%ADzk%C3%A9_Tatry%2C_chata_gener%C3%A1la_Milana_Rastislava_%C5%A0tef%C3%A1nika_-_krupicov%C3%A1_ka%C5%A1e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/N%C3%ADzk%C3%A9_Tatry%2C_chata_gener%C3%A1la_Milana_Rastislava_%C5%A0tef%C3%A1nika_-_krupicov%C3%A1_ka%C5%A1e.JPG/500px-N%C3%ADzk%C3%A9_Tatry%2C_chata_gener%C3%A1la_Milana_Rastislava_%C5%A0tef%C3%A1nika_-_krupicov%C3%A1_ka%C5%A1e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Semolina pudding with cocoa and butter","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AN%C3%ADzk%C3%A9_Tatry%2C_chata_gener%C3%A1la_Milana_Rastislava_%C5%A0tef%C3%A1nika_-_krupicov%C3%